⏺ Correcting labels clipped at an assay's detection limit

  (The results come from a scratch script on the Seagate drive. n30 is the suite version and hasn't run.)

  Looking for: an assay can't read values past its limit, so every molecule beyond the limit is recorded at the limit. Can those recorded labels be corrected so a model trained on them predicts new molecules better?

  Setup:
  - I clipped the herg_ki training labels on purpose. Every label above 6.86 pKi (the top 10% of training molecules, 94 of 941) was set to exactly 6.86. Test molecules kept their real labels.
  - The correction raises every label sitting at 6.86 by the same amount.
  - That amount estimates how far, on average, the true values sit above the limit. It is computed only from the clipped training data: the typical error of a model's predictions on the training molecules that weren't clipped.

  Results. herg_ki, RMSE on test molecules in pKi units, lower is better, mean of 3 cross-validation folds. Each row is one version of the training labels:

  ┌────────────────────────────┬────────┬──────────┬────────┬────────┐
