  I also ran herg_ki with 25% and 40% of training labels clipped, and caco2 with 25%. The corrected labels beat the uncorrected clipped labels on every model, every fold and every condition: 48 of 48 comparisons.

  Implication: clipping at a detection limit is the one noise mechanism where fixing the labels clearly works, and deleting the clipped molecules always makes predictions worse.


