  c19 — Importance weighting. Does weighting features by importance help?

  No, and the reason is structural, not empirical. lightgbm_gain writes exactly 0.0 for 66–78 features of a 250-feature hybrid, and zero times a standardised feature is a constant no tree can split on — so on a random forest the
  treatment is "delete 27% of the matrix and rescale". It cannot move a tree model by construction.

  It does work where distance matters: herg_ki 0.6196 → 0.6111 rmse, flab 0.4302 → 0.5081 spearman on kNN, with a shuffled-weights control that moves the right way. caco2: all ten schemes at or below unweighted for both rf and
  lightgbm.

  That is a good methods section — a null with a mechanism and a positive on the model class where the mechanism applies.

