  The headline: the hybrid's advantage is a function of how much search you let it do. Give it 48 configurations and it beats the ensemble, the best single representation, PCA and RFE. Give it 2 and it loses to the ensemble and to
  the best single representation.

  That is a defensible and interesting claim — the method is a search method, and its value scales with the search — but it needs one guard in the write-up: the comparison arms (ensemble, best single, PCA) do not get a search, so
  part of the gap is the hybrid taking a maximum over more draws. c11's numbers above are the leave-one-fold-out reselected ones, which taxes exactly that, so the effect survives the obvious correction — but it is the first thing
  a reviewer will ask.

